# Keeps the build context small and, more importantly, keeps host artefacts
# out of the images. Both Dockerfiles copy explicit paths rather than `COPY
# . .`, so nothing here is load-bearing for secrets — but `COPY apps/web
# ./apps/web` would otherwise pull in a stale .next or a host-built
# node_modules, which is how a build picks up artefacts that were never meant
# to ship. (Week 5 lost time to exactly that: a stale .next served content
# the database no longer had.)
#
# database/ is deliberately NOT ignored: the API image needs the migration
# and seed SQL at runtime.

# Dependencies — reinstalled inside the image for the right platform
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output — rebuilt inside the image
.next
**/.next
dist
**/dist
*.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets and local state. Never copied by either Dockerfile, excluded
# anyway so a future `COPY` cannot start leaking them.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.devdata

# Version control and CI
.git
.github
.gitattributes

# Local tooling and editor state
.claude
.vscode
.idea

# Test and coverage output
coverage
**/coverage
test-results

# Documentation and planning material — not needed to build or run
docs
*.docx
README.md
**/README.md

# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
